To determine how far the car can travel on 8 gallons of gas, we first need to find its fuel efficiency in miles per gallon (mpg). 

The car travels 192 miles on 6 gallons of gas. To find the mpg, we divide the total miles by the total gallons:  
\[
\text{mpg} = \frac{192 \text{ miles}}{6 \text{ gallons}} = 32 \text{ miles per gallon}
\]  

Next, we calculate the distance the car can travel on 8 gallons by multiplying the mpg by 8 gallons:  
\[
\text{Distance} = 32 \text{ mpg} \times 8 \text{ gallons} = 256 \text{ miles}
\]  

\boxed{256}

